{"leisure":{"w":"leisure","zh":["空閑","閑空","閑暇","餘暇"],"ipa":{"uk":"/ˈlɛʒə(ɹ)/","us":"/ˈlɛʒə(ɹ)/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"leyser","t":"inh"},{"l":"xno","f":"leisir","t":"der"},{"l":"fro","f":"loisir","t":"der","g":"to enjoy oneself"}],"text":"From Middle English leyser, from Anglo-Norman leisir, variant of Old French loisir (“to enjoy oneself”) (Modern French loisir survives as a noun), substantive use of a verb, from Latin licēre (“be permitted”). Displaced native Old English ǣmetta.","cog":[{"l":"fr","f":"loisir"}]}],"pos":[{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"Freedom provided by the cessation of activities.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"grp":0,"zh":"空閑"},{"d":"Free time, time free from work or duties.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"ex":["The desire of leisure is much more natural than of business and care.","This is why the mathematical arts were founded in Egypt; for there the priestly caste was allowed to be at leisure."],"grp":1,"zh":"空閑；閑空；閑暇"},{"d":"Time at one's command, free from engagement; convenient opportunity; hence, convenience; ease.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"ex":["He sigh'd, and had no leisure more to say."],"grp":1,"zh":"空閑；閑空；閑暇"}],"forms":[["pl","leisures"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"freedom provided","zh":["空閑"],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:loisir"],"it":["it:svago"],"es":["es:ocio"],"pt":["pt:lazer","pt:ócio"]}},{"label":"time free","zh":["空閑","閑空","閑暇","餘暇"],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:loisir","fr:temps libre"],"it":["it:agio","it:ozio","it:tempo libero"],"es":["es:ocio","es:tiempo libre"],"pt":["pt:lazer","pt:ócio","pt:tempo livre"]}}],"lx":{"fr:loisir":{"w":"loisir","p":"noun","g":"m","art":"le","pl":"loisirs","plArt":"les","ipa":"/lwa.ziʁ/","gl":"leisure, hobby","ety":{"chain":[{"l":"fro","f":"loisir","t":"inh"},{"l":"la","f":"licēre","t":"inh","lm":"licet","lmt":"inf","g":"to be allowed; to be permitted"},{"l":"itc-pro","f":"*likēt","t":"inh","unc":true},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*lik-eh₁-yéti","t":"inh"}],"